# A named subset of the learned sinks in ../sinks.satellites.bed (NYGC bwa-mem alignments of the 1000 Genomes 30x cohort to the
# GRCh38 analysis set; learned from 100 whole-file scans, engine fae1124): the fourth column names the class, so a fetch counts
# that class inside these intervals, and `ngsdose estimate` reports DYZ2.mass_Mb, DYZ2.reads and DYZ2.status for any counts
# file (scan or fetch) from the class's placements inside them (a placement bin counts only when all of it lies inside).
# Numbers below: held-out scans are the 1,648 cohort scans not among those 100; MB = bytes of the CRAM slices the intervals
# overlap with their containers' compression headers (as fetchplan counts them), median (range) over 13 NYGC .crai; reads
# per control 5' end is the class's reads inside / the control-region 5' ends.
# DYZ2: the male-specific HSat1B (the DYZ2 repeat of Yq12), as HSat1B reads land: mostly not on chrY (the 13 chrY HSat1B sinks
# hold 0.16% of it) but on autosomes, chrX and decoys. The 78 HSat1B sink intervals chosen on the 100 training scans (50 men, 50
# women) by: men's median >= 100 HSat1B reads, and women's median < 2% of men's: 66 autosomal, 7 on chrX, 3 on decoys, 2 on chrY.
# Measures: an index of male-specific (Y-derived) HSat1B: its part in these male-only intervals, about a quarter of the
# Y-derived part (21.7% of men's HSat1B), not the whole of it; near zero without Yq12 heterochromatin.
# Costs 34.3 MB (22.6-52.1). Held-out share of HSat1B: men 0.217, women 0.003; reads median men 313,740, women 587; per
# control 5' end, 69.6% of men lie above the largest female value.
# Truth: sex only (the HPRC release-2 assemblies rarely close Yq12: r 0.07 against annotated Y HSat1B, men, n = 27).
